  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "The Dlesk enterprises originated in Wheeling under Sylvan Dlesk, who combined development, investment and banking. His son Richard joined this established platform. State filings list him as vice-president of Dlesk, Inc., a company organised for non-residential construction. Sharick, Inc., a separate entity, held and leased buildings with his wife Sharon.\n\nThe couple later formed a Florida management company and retained their West Virginia connections. Their giving placed them in West Virginia University Foundation’s Woodburn Circle Society, reserved for major benefactors. His career shows quiet stewardship: Richard continued a second-generation commercial base through corporate office, jointly owned entities and regional investments, without cultivating the wider public profile associated with his father.",
    "html": "<p>The Dlesk enterprises originated in Wheeling under Sylvan Dlesk, who combined development, investment and banking. His son Richard joined this established platform. State filings list him as vice-president of Dlesk, Inc., a company organised for non-residential construction. Sharick, Inc., a separate entity, held and leased buildings with his wife Sharon.</p>\r\n<p>The couple later formed a Florida management company and retained their West Virginia connections. Their giving placed them in West Virginia University Foundation’s Woodburn Circle Society, reserved for major benefactors. His career shows quiet stewardship: Richard continued a second-generation commercial base through corporate office, jointly owned entities and regional investments, without cultivating the wider public profile associated with his father.</p>\r\n",
